{"content":[{"c":["NICOLAS, NICOLAUS*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["One of the seven men named in ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.6.5","r":"Acts.6.5","rawR":"Acts.6.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.6.5","value":"Acts.6.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 6:5"},", who was enlisted for service in the Jerusalem church in its early days. His duty as specified in ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.6.1-4","r":"Acts.6.1-4","rawR":"Acts.6.1-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.6.1-4","value":"Acts.6.1-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 6:1-4"}," was to direct the fair and equal distribution of food. Due to the use of terms in ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.6.1","r":"Acts.6.1","rawR":"Acts.6.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.6.1","value":"Acts.6.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 6:1"}," (“daily distribution” or “service”) and ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.6.2","r":"Acts.6.2","rawR":"Acts.6.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.6.2","value":"Acts.6.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:2"}," (“to distribute at tables” or “to serve”), these seven men traditionally have been called “deacons” (or “servers”)."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Nicolas, the last-named in the list, is identified as a proselyte. Thus, he was a Gentile convert to Judaism before he became a Christian. His name is Greek, and the city of Antioch is mentioned as his home. The NT writings provide no further information about him."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=DeaconDeaconess_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"DeaconDeaconess_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"DeaconDeaconess_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Deacon, Deaconess"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"NicolasNicolaus","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Acts 6:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.6.5","rawQueryValue":"Acts.6.5","sourceRefExact":"Acts.6.5"},{"anchorText":"Acts 6:1-4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.6.1-4","rawQueryValue":"Acts.6.1-4","sourceRefExact":"Acts.6.1-4"},{"anchorText":"Acts 6:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.6.1","rawQueryValue":"Acts.6.1","sourceRefExact":"Acts.6.1"},{"anchorText":"6:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.6.2","rawQueryValue":"Acts.6.2","sourceRefExact":"Acts.6.2"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"f6d1d97bcd54bd87edbd050f6bbc676051cc55aa92acc479ecc1f2f56c6e46d2","sourceItemName":"NicolasNicolaus","sourceItemOrder":140,"sourceMember":"Articles/N.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"NicolasNicolaus","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Nicolas, Nicolaus*","title":"Nicolas, Nicolaus*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}